{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books","id":1374011,"title":"Your favorite piece of fiction from the Ex3 books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-10T16:48:46-07:00","id":1374011,"title":"Your favorite piece of fiction from the Ex3 books?","content":"Game book chapter fiction or novellas, what's your favorite piece?<br /> <br /> Mine is the intro fiction for the Ex3 corebook. I like the whimsy of the mid-battle argument, a mighty Solar engine of destruction mortally offended over an insult to her culture's cuisine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T16:54:40-07:00","id":1374013,"title":"","content":"It's a tossup between the Strawmaiden Janest writeup and Volfer's fight in the burning building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T17:03:38-07:00","id":1374014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374013#post1374013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a tossup between the Strawmaiden Janest writeup and Volfer's fight in the burning building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say I've ever really like Volfer, but I like Janest for being the first Exigent we see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T17:06:38-07:00","id":1374016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374014#post1374014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say I've ever really like Volfer...</div> </div> </div> </div>What can I say? It's very evocative of Howard.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T17:20:52-07:00","id":1374018,"title":"","content":"The outro fiction. <br /> <br /> Though I hate the intro fiction. You have a Solar doing apparently <i>nothing</i> after the narration of Solars as world-shaking badasses, a Wyld Hunt dribbling into the fight, bizarre word choices that rip away from the tone, combat narration that doesn't actually tell you what's going on under all the flowery prose, and I personally hate the sudden divergence into food-talk during an assassination. <br /> And worst of all, it's the first thing a reader is going to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T21:56:56-07:00","id":1374062,"title":"","content":"I liked the bit set in Wu Jian, since the setting location interests me not just because it's full of competing martial arts 'gangs', but also for the hive-like aspects of the city allowing you to use changing height as an added method of travel, or fighting.<br /> <br /> But for my favorite piece of fiction so far, I'd have to say my vote also goes to Strawmaiden Janest... It's a very compelling in character examination of the 2nd Breath and just how meaningful it is for Exigents in particular, since in this case the God isn't powerful enough to survive the process, and even with his reasoning that the Wyld horde would kill him anyway, it makes for a noble sacrifice. And that is the kind of thing that one would expect to deeply affect a character, were you to see it in a prospective PC's background. And the threads of potential plot that all this forms in my mind as the story itself leaves us on a cliffhanger, is better than knowing any further concrete knowledge about the character.<br /> <br /> (Though I still wouldn't mind learning a bit more about Janest in the upcoming Exigents book)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T01:18:55-07:00","id":1374080,"title":"","content":"To keep this civil:<br /> <br /> I don't like the 3E chapter fiction. It's not to my taste. It doesn't have to be to my taste -- this is an agree to disagree thing.<br /> 1E had some nuggets of pure gold, but was mostly not to my taste -- I found most of it boring.<br /> I enjoyed literally every single 2E chapter comic. My favourite was the good ending from RotSE, closely followed by the intro comic in the Core, then the introduction of Lilith in Infernals.<br /> <br /> The 3E chapter fiction I hated least was probably Strawmaiden Janest. I'd grudgingly give it 5/10.<br /> <br /> I did a marginally more constructive <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1316045-johndoe-reads-the-chapter-fiction\">thread</a> about my opinions on the chapter fiction.<br /> <br /> I have no interest in the novellas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-11-2020, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T02:42:13-07:00","id":1374087,"title":"","content":"I really loved the fiction about Strawmaiden Janest. I don't think I read the others, maybe I should","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T09:46:16-07:00","id":1374157,"title":"","content":"Ex3 intro fiction is also my favorite. Between the longer overall length, lavish presentation, and the poetic writing style which mixes humor and seriousness together, it captured my imagination in a way that the shorter, more focused chapter fictions just can't compete with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 03-11-2020, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T11:50:04-07:00","id":1374180,"title":"","content":"I have to say my Favorite is the Opening Fiction... I really do love it... my close 2nd pick would be the Story of Strawmaiden Janest... But to be fair... I really do like all of the fiction in the Core Books. They all have something interesting to say, in my opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T12:53:33-07:00","id":1374198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374157#post1374157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ex3 intro fiction is also my favorite. Between the longer overall length, lavish presentation, and the poetic writing style which mixes humor and seriousness together, it captured my imagination in a way that the shorter, more focused chapter fictions just can't compete with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I vote for the most recently released novella as my favourite fiction so far. It's just got waaay more time to develop characters and have cool and interesting ideas play out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T20:34:40-07:00","id":1374483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374198#post1374198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I vote for the most recently released novella as my favourite fiction so far. It's just got waaay more time to develop characters and have cool and interesting ideas play out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't come to <i>this</i> thread expecting feedback on <i>that</i> piece of fiction. How nice.<br /> <br /> I'm not really objective regarding the fictions I wrote, but my favorite art piece <i>accompanying</i> a fiction I wrote precedes Chapter Six of The Realm. Beautiful, beautiful.<br /> <br /> Of the fictions I <i>didn't</i> write, Janest's is probably my favorite. Either that, or Tepet Arada's first-person fiction in <i>WFHW</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T02:11:50-07:00","id":1374520,"title":"","content":"I love fiction so this is a good topic for me. That said, other than the core, I haven't backed and so haven't read, any of the other Ex3 books so far. Just waiting on them being published and then going to buy. So I can't assess any of the quality of fic beyond the core.<br /> <br /> On the core, I liked the intro fiction, for various reasons I've enumerated elsewhere (and can be found by a forum search), but mainly because it seems like it was the only fiction that really had a good understanding of how to quickly draw sympathetic and archetypal characters with enough nuance and originality to suggest more depth of personality and create interest, and because it was the only fiction that actually managed to very much at all evoke the world of Exalted. Most of the other fiction was very much &quot;This could be happening in any fantasy world&quot;.<br /> <br /> The other bright spots I can remember which were *about* something interesting despite failing at execution (the above points of world and character evocation) were Shen's chap fic and Perfect Soul's moment of Exaltation chap fic. Conceptually they were good.<br /> <br /> Volfer's fiction I did not enjoy because it seemed to me to be trying to get me to buy the idea that crass, petty, immature and impulsive reactiveness as something that I would empathise with in its hero, and on an &quot;awesome audacious exploit&quot; that I found particularly lame. I guess it's like Alucard rather smartly mentioned, but for me in a less good way that suffers in comparison - it evokes audacious &quot;sword and sorcery&quot; heroes (Conan, Fahfrd etc) but Volfer suffers a little through comparison by seeming to just not be very cool and perhaps its author not seeming to have a good understanding of what makes a hero or maybe what humans in general cool (in the sense of radiating charisma, control, honor, genuine passion, charm, etc).<br /> <br /> Janest's fiction I found did not move me, as I fundamentally saw it as cynical and didactic - basically trying to upsell us on the idea of Exaltation and Exigency as a positive force in the world of Exalted and in the gameline of Exalted respectively, using pretty predictable tools and conventional writing. It seems like something put together for a purpose that seems too obvious and directed, rather than the product an author who can at least smartly disguise that purpose as a genuine, authentic and spontaneous exploration and reflection of mood, tone, character, etc with no ulterior purpose. (Even if this is age old, and simply feels more of a problem to me these days, I guess I am increasingly harsh on this as a problem of writing in our world. Lack of respect for readers as forming their opinions and beliefs, and a decline of writing that plausibly simply exists for the purpose of exploring the authors own feelings and ideas and genuinely conveying them, without much thought of trying to manipulate the audience, either to sell them something commercially or change their beliefs. If you're trying to do either of those manipulations, well, at least have enough respect for me to bother to hide it!). And again it's got that kind of &quot;This could be any fantasy setting&quot; quality.<br /> <br /> (Apologies of the above is too negative; no one take it too personally or seriously as a criticism of your personal taste).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 03-13-2020, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T03:46:11-07:00","id":1374535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374520#post1374520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Janest's fiction I found did not move me, as I fundamentally saw it as cynical and didactic - basically trying to upsell us on the idea of Exaltation and Exigency as a positive force in the world of Exalted and in the gameline of Exalted respectively, using pretty predictable tools and conventional writing. It seems like something put together for a purpose that seems too obvious and directed, rather than the product an author who can at least smartly disguise that purpose as a genuine, authentic and spontaneous exploration and reflection of mood, tone, character, etc with no ulterior purpose. (Even if this is age old, and simply feels more of a problem to me these days, I guess I am increasingly harsh on this as a problem of writing in our world. Lack of respect for readers as forming their opinions and beliefs, and a decline of writing that plausibly simply exists for the purpose of exploring the authors own feelings and ideas and genuinely conveying them, without much thought of trying to manipulate the audience, either to sell them something commercially or change their beliefs. If you're trying to do either of those manipulations, well, at least have enough respect for me to bother to hide it!). And again it's got that kind of &quot;This could be any fantasy setting&quot; quality.<br /> <br /> (Apologies of the above is too negative; no one take it too personally or seriously as a criticism of your personal taste).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a disconnect (between you and I certainly) as to what the chapter fiction is supposed to achieve.<br /> <br /> For me, it's about book-ending content. Breaking up the prose of the rulebook to refresh the mind. Foreshadowing the content to come in the next chapter, or recapping what has just been said -- presenting the dry textbook as a story.<br /> <br /> It's not about being interesting literature in its own right (though it certainly can be).<br /> <br /> I don't care for the WFHW fiction, but it walks us through the story of Dragon-Blooded as the rules present the world more clinically. What the rules tell us, the chapter fiction shows. That's what the chapter fiction (in my mind) is supposed to do, and WFHW does it well (perhaps too well because I find all the characters unsympathetic, insipid, boring, pathetic and evil, and reading the fiction makes me never want to play Dragon-Blooded -- but the chapter fiction does faithfully show us the world the body text describes, and it flows well).<br /> <br /> The point of the Janest story (in my mind, as a simple fan) is to bookend the Core. It's to summize what has been said (you play heroes of the gods against impossible odds), compliment the intro fiction (which with its style and tonal differences, I think it does superbly), and leave the reader wanting more from the gameline (the next chapter, so to speak).<br /> <br /> I agree with all of your literary criticisms (and if the story was less expositional and more nuanced I'd rate it more highly), but I think it's somewhat unfair to level them at a two page bookend. It's like complaining the Mona Lisa isn't as grand as the Sistine Chapel -- you're not wrong but that's not a realistic expectation.<br /> <br /> This is fiction put together for a specific purpose. That's literally what chapter fiction is and is supposed to be. It's not meant to be a genuine reflection of the author's soul -- writing for the sake of writting. It's meant to be an evocative summary of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T10:17:33-07:00","id":1374586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374520#post1374520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Janest's fiction I found did not move me, as I fundamentally saw it as cynical and didactic - basically trying to upsell us on the idea of Exaltation and Exigency as a positive force in the world of Exalted and in the gameline of Exalted respectively, using pretty predictable tools and conventional writing. It seems like something put together for a purpose that seems too obvious and directed, rather than the product an author who can at least smartly disguise that purpose as a genuine, authentic and spontaneous exploration and reflection of mood, tone, character, etc with no ulterior purpose. (Even if this is age old, and simply feels more of a problem to me these days, I guess I am increasingly harsh on this as a problem of writing in our world. Lack of respect for readers as forming their opinions and beliefs, and a decline of writing that plausibly simply exists for the purpose of exploring the authors own feelings and ideas and genuinely conveying them, without much thought of trying to manipulate the audience, either to sell them something commercially or change their beliefs. If you're trying to do either of those manipulations, well, at least have enough respect for me to bother to hide it!). And again it's got that kind of &quot;This could be any fantasy setting&quot; quality.<br /> <br /> (Apologies of the above is too negative; no one take it too personally or seriously as a criticism of your personal taste).</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I've got A Lot Of Thoughts on your view of creative writing, but I think a longform response would distract excessively from the purpose of this thread. Let me know if you're ever in the mood to hear a writer talk <i>at length </i>about cynicism, self-expression, and authorial intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T12:32:30-07:00","id":1374615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374535#post1374535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care for the WFHW fiction, but it walks us through the story of Dragon-Blooded as the rules present the world more clinically. What the rules tell us, the chapter fiction shows. That's what the chapter fiction (in my mind) is supposed to do, and WFHW does it well (perhaps too well because I find all the characters unsympathetic, insipid, boring, pathetic and evil, and reading the fiction makes me never want to play Dragon-Blooded -- but the chapter fiction does faithfully show us the world the body text describes, and it flows well).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yushoto and Kingfisher Swift aren\u2019t bad, River and Eshuvar are pretty dull, left hand Chamila is kind of both at once somehow. Tepet Arada, Cynis Cogen and Mnemon are pretty good though, makes me kind of wish Berit got a fiction. The old general with too many war stories, the former debauched party goer turned holy enforcer, the annoyed house matriarch juggling Night caste assassins with reorganizing one of her satrapies.<br /> <br /> Excepting maybe Mnemon I don\u2019t think any of them are depicted as evil though. The anathema they\u2019re hunting don\u2019t want to bring the fight to their village because the Realm is known to give zero fucks when anathema are concerned. River then becomes upset at the implication that their hunt would kill a village of innocent mortals in pursuit of anathema, but concedes that the Realm is known for doing such things so it\u2019s a reasonable precaution for the anathema to take.<br /> <br /> If you got it from the Kickstarter I really would give the novella a try though, it\u2019s much better than most of the corebook stuff because it\u2019s an actual story with fun dragonblooded heroes squaring off against ancient forgotten monsters rather than just a single scene of one character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T08:12:41-07:00","id":1374760,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Just a reminder.<br /> This is a thread about people's *favourite* pieces of fiction in Ex3, it's not like we don't have an entire Exalted forum. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-14-2020, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T13:50:13-07:00","id":1374795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374760#post1374760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Just a reminder.<br /> This is a thread about people's favourite pieces of fiction in Ex3, it's not like we don't have an entire Exalted forum. </span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Is the thread against the rules? Or is that a 'get back on topic' prodding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T14:47:30-07:00","id":1374810,"title":"","content":"It's just a little prodding. I initially put the emphisis on favourite but it got lost in the bolded mod text, edited for clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T23:22:39-07:00","id":1374885,"title":"","content":"From the corebook, the Janest piece like a lot of folks. I think it is the one that most fits to me the &quot;This is new and awesome and wonderous&quot; that I think the original 1e intro fiction did. It also came with the illustration that I think just really sold the entire scene great.<br /> <br /> I also liked the the one about the Seven Degreed Surgeon of Black Maladies. Because it was just such a bizarre piece of slice-of-life ficiton in such an exotic setting. I like the idea of mundane issues in absurd situations in comedy and fiction in general, so that might be why it stood out so much to me. It had this Glenn Cook feel to it I liked a lot.<br /> <br /> Out of the corebook, I think I liked the strucutre of the fiction in teh Dragon-Blooded book a lot. With special shout-outs to the intro and outro, the fiction from the Empress' point of view, and also the one with Mnemon had one of my favorite lines the ficiton. (&quot;The Dragons provide.&quot;). Plus the one wiht the monk kicking the evry living shit out of a god was cool too.<br /> <br /> The fiction in <b>Arms of the Chosen</b> and <b>The Realm</b> are fine, but I admit didn't stand out as much fo rme in either's case. IN thsoe I would say the one from the satrapy chapter of <b>The Realm</b> though is rpetty cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T18:44:53-07:00","id":1375526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374011-your-favorite-piece-of-fiction-from-the-ex3-books?p=1374198#post1374198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I vote for the most recently released novella as my favourite fiction so far. It's just got waaay more time to develop characters and have cool and interesting ideas play out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your praise got me to read the DB novella and I have to say I really enjoyed it, it's now tied with the Core intro for my favorite. I might have to do more of this reading-fiction-that-isn't-in-the-splat-books thing...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}